The Only Resource of a "Poor Mountain Region": Human Life (Blood Exports)\par
\par
During the medieval and early modern periods, Switzerland was an impoverished agricultural nation nestled deep in the Alps, devoid of arable land and natural resources.\par
\par
To survive, they discovered their most powerful export: disciplined, mountain-hardened, and contract-abiding young men\emdash "mercenaries" (professional combat groups).\par
\par
They systematically and commercially dispatched mercenaries to rulers across Europe, from the King of France to the Pope (the Swiss Guard at the Vatican remains a relic of this), earning foreign currency.\par
\par
