The Brilliant Shift from "Selling Flesh" to "Selling Systems and IP"\par
\par
In the mid-19th century, reflecting on the tragedy of their citizens being ground up in foreign wars, official mercenary supplies were banned.\par
\par
However, the pivot engineered by Swiss elites was brilliant: "Let's stop bleeding by exporting humans. Instead, let's shift to a system where we export and provide 'weapons/intellectual property,' 'finance/assets,' and 'international neutral platforms (turf)' used in foreign wars, earning foreign currency without risk." This was the birth of their modern business model.\par
